If $\Delta > 0$ there are two stationary points: a local maximum and a local minimum.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (-2.9,0) -- (2.9,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-2.0) -- (0,2.0) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-2.1:2.1, smooth, variable=\x] plot (\x, {0.45*(\x*\x*\x - 3*\x)});
\filldraw (-1,0.9) circle (2pt);
\filldraw (1,-0.9) circle (2pt);
\draw (-1,-0.12) -- (-1,0.12);
\draw (1,-0.12) -- (1,0.12);
\node[below left] at (-1,-0.12) {$x_1$};
\node[above right] at (1,0.12) {$x_2$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

If $\Delta = 0$ there is one stationary point, a **horizontal point of inflection**, and no turning points.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (-1.7,0) -- (3.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-2.0) -- (0,2.0) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-0.6:2.6, smooth, variable=\x] plot (\x, {0.4*(\x-1)*(\x-1)*(\x-1) + 0.5});
\filldraw (1,0.5) circle (2pt);
\draw (1,-0.12) -- (1,0.12);
\node[below right] at (1,-0.12) {$x_1$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

If $\Delta < 0$ there are no stationary points, so the cubic is increasing everywhere or decreasing everywhere.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (-2.5,0) -- (2.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-2.2) -- (0,2.2) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-1.6:1.6, smooth, variable=\x] plot (\x, {0.2*(\x*\x*\x + 3*\x)});
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

For a negative cubic ($a < 0$) the pattern reverses: the curve falls, rises between $x_1$ and $x_2$, then falls again.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (-2.9,0) -- (2.9,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-2.0) -- (0,2.0) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-2.1:2.1, smooth, variable=\x] plot (\x, {0.45*(3*\x - \x*\x*\x)});
\filldraw (-1,-0.9) circle (2pt);
\filldraw (1,0.9) circle (2pt);
\draw (-1,-0.12) -- (-1,0.12);
\draw (1,-0.12) -- (1,0.12);
\node[above left] at (-1,0.12) {$x_1$};
\node[below right] at (1,-0.12) {$x_2$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
